 3.037 1.505 4.166.645 1.102-.833 1.344-2.204.672-4.166l-5.618-16.718 14.353-10.32c1.666-1.183 2.338-2.42 1.908-3.764-.43-1.29-1.693-1.935-3.763-1.908l-17.605.108-5.348-16.8C34.308 4.496 33.34 3.5 31.944 3.5c-1.372 0-2.34.995-2.984 2.984L23.61 23.283l-17.605-.108c-2.07-.027-3.333.618-3.763 1.908-.457 1.344.242 2.58 1.909 3.763l14.352 10.321-5.617 16.718c-.672 1.962-.43 3.333.672 4.166Z"></path></svg> </li> </ol></div></div> <div class="review-header svelte-1nf834u"><time class="date svelte-1nf834u" datetime="2025-01-06T04:03:56.000Z">01/06/2025</time>  <div class="multiline-clamp svelte-1r39353" style="--mc-lineClamp: var(--defaultClampOverride, 1);" role="text"> <span class="multiline-clamp__text svelte-1r39353"><span class="author svelte-1nf834u">cognitive gears</span></span> </div></div></div> <div class="content svelte-1nf834u">  <div class="truncate-wrapper svelte-1b6lxg0"><p data-testid="truncate-text" dir="auto" class="content svelte-1b6lxg0" style="--lines: 3; --line-height: var(--lineHeight, 16); --link-length: 4;"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->I’ve tried a few habit apps, and absolutely love using this one so far. The user experience is extremely intuitive and easy to use, and has (almost) all the features I was looking for. Just as an example, the Shortcuts integration is great for me - I was able to integrate HabitKit into an existing Shortcut I was using for recording a daily journal, and so now recording one will also automatically mark the habit complete for the day too. The widgets are really nice too and improve the overall interaction.All that said, there are just a few additional features I’d like to see. First, a MacOS version of the app would be great, though I can confirm that it does work to install the iOS version. However, it would really be awesome if it could sync to iCloud both to make this actually usable, as well as to make it easy when you get a new device. There is an export / import feature for this but this would make it a lot. Lee seamless. Finally, it would be nice to have additional Shortcuts support - the ability to look at past completions / streaks, change completion for other dates, export / import from Shortcut, etc.With that list, why did I still give it 5 stars? Because even as-is it is incredibly useful and I would recommend it to everyone even without these features (though they would be great!)<!-- HTML_TAG_END --></p> </div>  <div class="developer-response-container svelte-1nf834u"><span class="developer-response-heading svelte-1nf834u">Developer Response</span>   <div class="truncate-wrapper svelte-1b6lxg0"><p data-testid="truncate-text" dir="auto" class="content svelte-1b6lxg0" style="--lines: 1; --line-height: var(--lineHeight, 16); --link-length: 4;"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->Hey! Thanks for the awesome review and your feedback. Mac support and cross-device sync are on the roadmap!I really appreciate that you still rated it 5 stars even though it doesn't have every feature you wish for!<!-- HTML_TAG_END --></p> </div> </div></div></div>  <dialog data-testid="dialog" class="svelte-1p01z7" id="" aria-hidden="true"><div data-testid="content-modal" class="content-modal-container svelte-1ih6d3u" dir="auto"><div class="button-container svelte-1ih6d3u"><button data-testid="content-modal-close-button" class="close-button svelte-1ih6d3u" type="button" aria-label="Close"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18" aria-hidden="true" data-testid="content-modal-close-button-svg"><path d="M1.2 18C.6 18 0 17.5 0 16.8c0-.4.1-.6.4-.8l7-7-7-7c-.3-.2-.4-.5-.4-.8C0 .5.6 0 1.2 0c.3 0 .6.1.8.3l7 7 7-7c.2-.2.5-.3.8-.3.6 0 1.2.5 1.2 1.2 0 .3-.1.6-.4.8l-7 7 7 7c.2.2.4.5.4.8 0 .7-.6 1.2-1.2 1.2-.3 0-.6-.1-.8-.3l-7-7-7 7c-.2.1-.5.3-.8.3z"></path></svg></button> </div> <div class="header-container svelte-1ih6d3u"><h1 data-testid="content-modal-title" class="title svelte-1ih6d3u">Almost perfect</h1> </div> <div class="content-container svelte-1ih6d3u"><div class="container svelte-1nf834u is-detail-view" aria-