l under the same habit. Say you want to add a yoga habit for each day, but want reminders at 2:00pm on certain days and 3:00pm on other days for those with varying schedules. I also think sub-habit/task would be an interesting game changer. Say you’re trying to incorporate an entire morning routine habit, you can just label the habit morning routine, and you can click it to open, add a sub-habit/task, like make bed, brush teeth, do skin care, and once you check off all three of those things, it will complete that habit for the day. I feel like this would help with lessening the amount of habits you have to make when one habit can incorporate many things you want to do!<!-- HTML_TAG_END --> <div class="developer-response-container svelte-1nf834u"><div class="developer-response-header svelte-1nf834u"><span class="developer-response-heading svelte-1nf834u">Developer Response</span> <time class="date svelte-1nf834u" datetime="2024-07-31T09:05:58.000Z">07/31/2024</time></div> <!-- HTML_TAG_START -->Hey there,Thank you so much for the awesome review and your feedback. I am currently working on a cross-device sync functionality and hope to release it this year!More reminder/notification configuration options are also on the roadmap and will be implemented with a future version of the app.Ultimately, some form of "categories" will come with the next big update, so very soon. Stay tuned for that.Thanks for the great points!<!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div></p></div> </div> </div> </dialog> </div></li>   <li class="shelf-grid__list-item svelte-13b6ljx" data-test-id="shelf-grid-list-item-3" data-index="3" aria-hidden="true"><div class="svelte-13b6ljx"><div class="container svelte-1nf834u" aria-labelledby="review-13432617886-title" dir="ltr"><div class="header svelte-1nf834u"><div class="title-and-rating-container svelte-1nf834u"> <div class="multiline-clamp svelte-1r39353" style="--mc-lineClamp: var(--defaultClampOverride, 1);" role="text"> <span class="multiline-clamp__text svelte-