chGroup":null,"seeAllAction":null,"footerTitle":null,"footerAction":null,"eyebrow":null,"eyebrowArtwork":null,"footerStyle":null,"title":"Ratings & Reviews","titleArtwork":null,"subtitle":null,"isHorizontal":false,"isHidden":false,"rowsPerColumn":null,"background":{"type":"none"},"contentsMetadata":{"type":"none"},"isPersonalized":false,"shouldFilterApps":false},{"$kind":"Shelf","impressionMetrics":{"fields":{"id":"23","name":"","impressionType":"ratingsDetails","idType":"sequential","impressionIndex":2}},"contentType":"reviews","marker":null,"items":[{"$kind":"Review","id":"12150441065","title":"Almost perfect","date":"2025-01-06T04:03:56.000Z","dateText":"* null *","contents":"I’ve tried a few habit apps, and absolutely love using this one so far. The user experience is extremely intuitive and easy to use, and has (almost) all the features I was looking for. Just as an example, the Shortcuts integration is great for me - I was able to integrate HabitKit into an existing Shortcut I was using for recording a daily journal, and so now recording one will also automatically mark the habit complete for the day too. The widgets are really nice too and improve the overall interaction.\n\nAll that said, there are just a few additional features I’d like to see. First, a MacOS version of the app would be great, though I can confirm that it does work to install the iOS version. However, it would really be awesome if it could sync to iCloud both to make this actually usable, as well as to make it easy when you get a new device. There is an export / import feature for this but this would make it a lot. Lee seamless. Finally, it would be nice to have additional Shortcuts support - the ability to look at past completions / streaks, change completion for other dates, export / import from Shortcut, etc.\n\nWith that list, why did I still give it 5 stars? Because even as-is it is incredibly useful and I would recommend it to everyone even without these features (though they would be great!)","rating":5,"reviewerName":"cognitive gears","dateAuthorText":"* null * · cognitive gears","response":{"$kind":"Response","id":"49799617","contents":"Hey! Thanks for the awesome review and your feedback. Mac support and cross-device sync are on the roadmap!\nI really appreciate that you still rated it 5 stars even though it doesn't have every feature you wish for!","date":"2025-01-20T14:06:50.000Z","dateText":"* null *"}},{"$kind":"Review","id":"12934585259","title":"One of the best habit tracking apps - but NEEDS iOS Reminders integration and maybe APIs exposed ?","date":"2025-07-25T12:39:34.000Z","dateText":"* null *","contents":"This is by far the most visually appealing app. I was actually going to develop my own app which was similar to this, where it had the altair heatmap chart. But this goes beyond my initial idea and also has step counts/tiered counting. Moreover, the ease of completing a task with a tap, setting of reminders, color coding and the availability to switch between three different views is exactly what I needed.\n\nThis is way better than todoist, it is simple and intuitive. Most other apps have a lot of clutter and have too many details and clunky interfaces.\n\nOne important feature that is missing though is its integration with Calendar and Reminders. Not just that, PLEASE expose APIs to interact with the data, this would have a limited use case, but still could be very useful. For example, one could ingest their daily step count and automatically mark a habit. Another example is that say if I want to block a particular app unless I do X, it could allow it to do so. Lets say that I have a habit like “no scrolling videos in the morning for 2 hours”, I should be able to enforce this and mark the habit only when certain conditions outside the app are met - I know this is a little outside the scope of this app and probably would fit into another “habit enforcer” app that could integrate with this, but in any case this requires REST APIs to be exposed. I would love to partner with the dev and work on this idea.","rating":4,"reviewerName":"smartraccoon1111","dateAuthorText":"* null * · smartraccoon1111"},{"$kind":"Review","id":"11526306665","title":"Great Simple App, Great Developer, Some Limitations","date":"2024-07-23T16:44:59.000Z","dateText":"* null *","contents":"I really love how simple and easy this app is to use. The pricing is also extremely reasonable for $0.99 when most apps charge way more just for some basic functions. I think it would be great if we would were able to create our own account so we can sync progress across different devices. \n\nI have ADHD and this app really helps me stay motivated and manage my executive dysfunction because I have to gamify EVERYTHING just to do simple things. I like how we are able to select different days for when we want to track a habit, but I wish we could select different reminder times for different days as well under the same habit. Say you want to add a yoga habit for each day, but want reminders at 2:00pm on certain days and 3:00pm on other days for those with varying schedules.\n\n I also think sub-habit/task would be an interesting game changer. Say you’re trying to incorporate an entire morning routine habit, you can just label the habit morning routine, and you can click it to open, add a sub-habit/task, like make bed, brush teeth, do skin care, and once you check off all three of those things, it will complete that habit for the day. I feel like this would help with lessening the amount of habits you have to make when one habit can incorporate many things you want to do!","rating":5,"reviewerName":"LegendaryPink","dateAuthorText":"* null * · LegendaryPink","response":{"$kind":"Response","id":"45648942","contents":"Hey there,\n\nThank you so much for the awesome review and your feedback. I am currently working on a cross-device sync functionality and hope to release it this year!\nMore reminder/notification configuration options are also on the roadmap and will be implemented with a future version of the app.\nUltimately, some form of \"categories\" will come with the next big update, so very soon. Stay tuned for that.\n\nThanks for the great points!","date":"2024-07-31T09:05:58.000Z","dateText":"* null *"}},{"$kind":"Review","id":"13432617886","title":"A Game Changer","date":"2025-11-23T18:11:52.000Z","dateText":"* null *","contents":"I recently turned started using a minimalist phone setup to help me to be more productive. A key part of the design was adding HabitKit widgets to my home screen. It's very motivating to see your habit history packed into a beautiful little chart, with the ability to check off (or increment) habits without having to open the app. After making these changes to my phone, this past week has been the most productive week of my life, and I sincerely believe HabitKit has been the main reason for that. \n\nThe support is also incredible. I reached out to the solo developer via email, asking him about 2 different features I was hoping he could add to the app. 2 days later, he got back to me, in a very friendly and well-thought-out email. In this email, he told me that he had already been working on adding the first feature, and the other had been added to his todo list. Given that he is a solo developer, and also working on another up-and-coming app at the same time, I'd say his support services are the best I've ever seen, from any app on the app store.","rating":5,"reviewerName":"Cole Lentini","dateAuthorText":"* null * · Cole Lentini"},{"$kind":"Review","id":"13695520678","title":"Almost perfect - Few updates needed","date":"2026-01-31T05:04:24.000Z","dateText":"* null *","contents":"I first downloaded HabitKit in the ending of March 2025. I bought the lifetime premium version. When I first downloaded the app, it didn't have an option for putting your own emojis for habits, which was really frustrating. I'm very happy that they finally put an emoji update. I was tired of using a dog bone for my seafood habit. My issue with the new update is that you can't change the skin color of the emojis. It's also disappointing that you can't choose a set of Crayola like colors for your habits including brown, instead of the preset pastel colors that is given. No true red or solid purples just a pastel palette for everything... I also think that the counter for 1, 5, 10 , 15 shouldn't be there. I think that instead the only option should be to set your own number of \"Pages read\" for each habit. It would look much better for the eyes that way. Or at least give the option to turn it off and only have your own preset number. I also think that the HabitKit wrapped should be worded better and upgraded. Besides those things, this is a decent app for habit tracking. I do also believe having a bad habit tracker section or page would be great, and helpful for separation of good and bad habits. Plus not being able to sync to iCloud is hella wack. I can only give 2 stars because I know it could be better.","rating":2,"reviewerName":"Angiestarlit","dateAuthorText":"* null * · Angiestarlit"},{"$kind":"Review","id":"14089093879","title":"Absolutely Love!","date":"2026-05-21T12:22:44.000Z","dateText":"* null *","contents":"I love this app for tracking my habits! I’ve tried other apps and none of them were as good as this one. I like that I can choose a dark background and because of all the bright colors, it looks beautiful. I have the PRO version and o definitely think it’s worth the money; and it’s not expensive at all. I can track as many habits as I want to, and I can archive them when I want to stop tracking them (but it doesn’t delete them so I can “unarchive”them if I want to start tracking that habit again. I would like to suggest a couple of things that I think could make it better…first, I’d love to be able to set an alarm for my habits to remind me to do some of them. I’d also like to have a bigger color selection to choose from. The colors it has are beautiful and vibrant but I’d just like to add some more shades (because I track a lot of habits). I love the icons too, and the fact that I can reorder my habits at any time. All in all, it’s a fantastic app and I use it everyday! I’d definitely recommend for EVERYONE to get the pro version, and start tracking your habits! I’ve gotten a lot more consistent since I started using this app!","rating":4,"reviewerName":"a2thaMb","dateAuthorText":"* null * · a2thaMb"},{"$kind":"Review","id":"13690973300","title":"The Perfect App For What I Needed","date":"2026-01-30T00:21:45.000Z","dateText":"* null *","contents":"This app on my phone has been insanely helpful and so easy to use. I can track anything going on in my life and then easily look back over the history of my habit. Things like how frequently I’m vacuuming or if I took my medication each day or week. Every time I login and track my habits it also reminds me of things I might not have done yet like…oh I haven’t done that thing yet today. So I often get up to start or finish something because I see that it isn’t checked off for the day. \n\nWhat makes this app better than others I was looking at is that I’m 100% choosing my own categories and specific tasks. So my weird and wonderful lists are tailored perfectly to me, and there isn’t anything extraneous. \n\nThe only complaint I have is that the data is only on your device. So I can see and use it on my phone but I can’t pull it up on my tablet or computer. I reached out to the developers and they say they hope to change this in the future. So fingers crossed, this app could get even better.","rating":5,"reviewerName":"Hattrik103","dateAuthorText":"* null * · Hattrik103"},{"$kind":"Review","id":"11196441680","title":"Fantastic Habit Tracker from a Responsive Developer","date":"2024-04-24T19:09:15.000Z","dateText":"* null *","contents":"The app is an intuitive, visually pleasing way to track your habits. It does a great job of allowing users to customize their habits while not crowding the ui or creating a convoluted user experience. Overall, it is a near-perfect habit tracker with a nice minimalist aesthetic\n\nAlso, the developer shows a lot of respect for the users of the app. I wrote to them regarding some functionality that I was hoping they would add and they quickly wrote back to let me know they were working on that. A couple months later they reached out to let me know they were rolling out that feature! In my experience, it is hard to find a developer that is so genuinely responsive to user feedback\n\nLastly, the app, which does have a premium option, makes the non-premium version actually worthwhile to use and offers the premium version via both subscription and one-time-purchase. Both of those are big pluses in my book!","rating":5,"reviewerName":"AngletonReviews","dateAuthorText":"* null * · AngletonReviews","response":{"$kind":"Response","id":"44884920","contents":"Thank you so much for the awesome review, I really appreciate your support and am happy that you like my app and development!","date":"2024-06-27T10:11:28.000Z","dateText":"* null *"}}],"url":null,"mergeWhenFetched":false,"fetchStrategy":"onPageLoad","batchGroup":null,"seeAllAction":null,"footerTitle":null,"footerAction":null,"eyebrow":null,"eyebrowArtwork":null,"footerStyle":null,"titleArtwork":null,"subtitle":null,"isHorizontal":false,"isHidden":false,"rowsPerColumn":null,"background":{"type":"none"},"contentsMetadata":{"type":"none"},"isPersonalized":false,"shouldFilterApps":false,"id":"ReviewsPage.ShelfId.helpful","presentationHints":{"isSortable":true,"isSeeAllContext":true}}],"title":null,"presentationOptions":[],"isIncomplete":false,"pageMetrics":{"$kind":"PageMetrics","instructions":[],"custom":{}},"$kind":"ReviewsPage","trailingNavBarAction":null,"adamId":"6443918070","nextPage":{"url":"x-as3-internal:/reviews/shelf/6443918070/helpful","remainingContent":[],"nextHref":"/v1/catalog/us/apps/6443918070/reviews?l=en-US&offset=8","profile":